 Create a Repository with at Least Three Meaningful Commits
Git repository is used to store and manage project files. Commits help track changes made to the project.
Git Commands:

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial project setup"

git add .
git commit -m "Added HTML structure"

git add .
git commit -m "Added CSS styling"

git log --oneline
```

Conclusion: These commands create a Git repository with three meaningful commits to track project changes.

